1
00:00:00,352 --> 00:00:14,080
Section 2 You will hear a restaurant manager talking to a small group of new staff who are starting work as kitchen assistants in a restaurant.

2
00:00:14,523 --> 00:00:39,327
First, you have some time to look at questions 11 to 16.

3
00:00:39,770 --> 00:01:08,560
[BLANK_AUDIO] Now listen carefully and answer questions 11 to 16.

4
00:01:08,640 --> 00:01:10,390
Good morning everyone.

5
00:01:10,470 --> 00:01:20,170
My name is Joy Parkins and I'm the restaurant manager and I understand that none of you have had any previous experiences kitchen assistants.

6
00:01:20,228 --> 00:01:27,200
Well, you might be feeling a bit nervous now but most of our kitchen assistants say they enjoy the work.

7
00:01:27,264 --> 00:01:31,711
Okay, they might get shouted at sometimes, but it's nothing personal,

8
00:01:31,711 --> 00:01:38,080
and they're pleased that they have so many different things to do, which means they never get bored.

9
00:01:38,144 --> 00:01:41,447
And I'll tell you straight away that if you do well,

10
00:01:41,447 --> 00:01:47,440
we might think about moving you up and giving you some more responsibility.

11
00:01:47,506 --> 00:01:53,040
Right, well, you've all shown up on time, which is an excellent start.

12
00:01:53,109 --> 00:01:58,244
Now, I'm glad to see none of you have unsuitable footwear, so that's good.

13
00:01:58,313 --> 00:02:03,025
You need to be careful as the floors can get very wet and slippery.

14
00:02:03,095 --> 00:02:11,043
Those of you with long hair, I've got it well out of the way, but some of you all need to remove your rings and bracelets,

15
00:02:11,043 --> 00:02:18,760
just put them somewhere safer today, and remember to leave them at home tomorrow as they can be a safety hazard.

16
00:02:18,838 --> 00:02:22,737
Now it's going to be a busy day for you all today.

17
00:02:22,815 --> 00:02:28,470
We don't have any tables free for this evening, and only a few for lunch.

18
00:02:28,546 --> 00:02:31,760
Fortunately, we've got our head chef back.

19
00:02:31,837 --> 00:02:37,197
He was away on holiday all last week, which meant the other chefs had extra work.

20
00:02:37,259 --> 00:02:44,456
Now, I'll tell you a bit more about the job in a minute, but first some general regulations.

21
00:02:44,544 --> 00:02:52,893
For all of you, whatever your age, there's some equipment you mustn't use until you've been properly trained,

22
00:02:52,893 --> 00:02:59,131
like the waste disposal system for example, for health and safety reasons.

23
00:02:59,221 --> 00:03:07,019
Then I think there are two of you here who are under 18, that's Emma and Jake isn't it?

24
00:03:07,108 --> 00:03:09,080
Right, so for you two,

25
00:03:09,080 --> 00:03:18,581
the meat slicer is out of bounds and of course none of you are allowed to use the electric mixer until you've been shown how it works.

26
00:03:18,663 --> 00:03:27,440
Now you may have heard that this can be a stressful job and I have to say that can be true.

27
00:03:27,494 --> 00:03:30,461
You'll be working an eight hour day for the first week,

28
00:03:30,461 --> 00:03:36,240
though you'll have the chance to do overtime after that as well if you want to.

29
00:03:36,317 --> 00:03:41,320
But however long the hours are, you'll get a break in the middle.

30
00:03:41,385 --> 00:03:49,491
What you will find is that you're on your feet all day long, lifting and carrying, so if you're not fit now you soon will be.

31
00:03:49,557 --> 00:03:57,549
You'll find you don't have much chance to take it easy when someone tells you to do something you need to do it straight away,

32
00:03:57,549 --> 00:04:41,280
but at least we do have a very efficient air conditioning system compared with some kitchens.

33
00:04:41,305 --> 00:04:43,483
Before you hear the rest of the talk, you have some time to look at questions 17 to 20.

34
00:04:43,508 --> 00:04:45,060
Now let me tell you about some of the people you need to know.

35
00:04:45,134 --> 00:04:52,700
So as I said, I'm Joy Parkins and I decide who does watch during the day and how long they work for.

36
00:04:52,759 --> 00:05:01,540
I'll be trying to get you to work with as many different people in the kitchen as possible so that you learn while you're on the job.

37
00:05:01,616 --> 00:05:05,801
One person whose name you must remember is David Field.

38
00:05:05,877 --> 00:05:09,868
If you injure yourself at all, even if it's really minor,

39
00:05:09,868 --> 00:05:16,746
you must report to him and he'll make sure the incident is recorded and you get the appropriate treatment.

40
00:05:16,811 --> 00:05:23,848
He's trained to give basic treatment to staff himself or he'll send you off somewhere else if necessary.

41
00:05:23,917 --> 00:05:25,787
Then there's Dexter Will's.

42
00:05:25,857 --> 00:05:31,126
He's the person you need to see if you smash a plate or something like that.

43
00:05:31,196 --> 00:05:34,539
Don't just leave it and hope no one will notice.

44
00:05:34,608 --> 00:05:40,737
It's really important to get things noted and replaced, or there could be problems later.

45
00:05:40,806 --> 00:05:42,933
And finally, there's Mike Smith.

46
00:05:42,992 --> 00:05:47,810
He's the member of staff who takes care of all the stores of perishables.

47
00:05:47,892 --> 00:05:57,500
So, if you notice we're getting low in flour or sugar or something, make sure you let him know so he can put in an order.

48
00:05:57,579 --> 00:06:00,980
Okay, now the next thing we need to call...

49
00:06:01,388 --> 00:06:13,219
That is the end of section 2.

50
00:06:13,627 --> 00:06:33,617
You now have half a minute to check your answers.

51
00:06:34,025 --> 00:06:43,000
Now turn to Section 3.